  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the target of the abusive judgment",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'stupid you are, breed you should not' because the text directly addresses the viewer as the recipient of the insult. The phrase 'you are' and 'you should not' explicitly deictically refers to the user, making them the target of the judgment. This projection is reinforced by the visual of Yoda, who is mapped as the source of this judgment, creating a direct address to the user.",
